  "title": "Forth Bridge",
  "summary": "The Forth Bridge carries the railway across the Forth estuary in eastern Scotland, linking Fife with Edinburgh. Built from 1882, it opened on 4 March 1890 as a cantilever bridge with the world's longest spans (541 m). It still carries passengers and freight and was inscribed by UNESCO in 2015.",
